  JOURNAL   Mol Microbiol 6 (23), 3543-3550 (1992)
   PUBMED   1282192
  REMARK    FUNCTION, AND DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE.
REFERENCE   4  (residues 1 to 140)
  AUTHORS   Englert,C. and Pfeifer,F.
  TITLE     Analysis of gas vesicle gene expression in Haloferax mediterranei
            reveals that GvpA and GvpC are both gas vesicle structural proteins
  JOURNAL   J Biol Chem 268 (13), 9329-9336 (1993)
   PUBMED   7683649
  REMARK    INDUCTION.
REFERENCE   5  (residues 1 to 140)
  AUTHORS   Roder,R. and Pfeifer,F.
  TITLE     Influence of salt on the transcription of the gas-vesicle genes of
            Haloferax mediterranei and identification of the endogenous
            transcriptional activator gene
  JOURNAL   Microbiology (Reading) 142 (Pt 7), 1715-1723 (1996)
   PUBMED   8757736
  REMARK    INDUCTION BY SALT.;
            STRAIN=ATCC 33500 / DSM 1411 / JCM 8866 / NBRC 14739 / NCIMB 2177 /
            R-4
COMMENT     On Apr 26, 2005 this sequence version replaced gi:282678.
            [FUNCTION] A minor component of the gas vesicle (GV), may play a
            role in transcription and/or RNA stability and/or in GV assembly.
            Gas vesicles are small, hollow, gas filled protein structures found
            in some microorganisms. They allow positioning of halobacteria at
            the optimal depth for growth in the poorly aerated shallow brine
            pools of their habitat. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O51968}.
            [FUNCTION] Expression of a 9.5 kb mc-vac DNA fragment containing 2
            divergently transcribed regions
            (gvpD-gvpE-gvpF-gvpG-gvpH-gvpI-gvpJ-gvpK-gvpL-gvpM and
            gvpA-gvpC-gvpN-gvpO) allows H.volcanii to produce gas vesicles.
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:1282192, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1404376,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:8757736}.
            [SUBUNIT] Forms homodimers, forms a GvpN-GvpO heterodimer,
            interacts with GvpC, GvpF, GvpI and GvpL, might interact with GvpA.
            {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O51968}.
            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Gas vesicle {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O51968}.
            Cytoplasm {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O51968}.
            [INDUCTION] Expressed from a single promoter upstream of gvpA; most
            transcripts stop at the gvpA terminator, with low read-through into
            downstream gvpC-gvpN-gvpO. Expression starts in early stationary
            phase and is maximal in stationary phase (PubMed:7683649,
            PubMed:8757736). Highly expressed in 25% salt, poorly expressed in
            15% salt, no gas vesicles are formed at 15% salt (PubMed:8757736).
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:7683649, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8757736}.
            [DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE] No longer makes gas vesicles in H.volcanii;
            cells translate GvpA but do not make gas vesicles.
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:1282192, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1404376}.
            [MISCELLANEOUS] Encoded in a 14-gene locus called mc-vac.
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:1282192, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1404376}.
            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the gas vesicle GvpO family. {ECO:0000305}.
