            STRAIN=CB03234
            Publication Status: Online-Only
REFERENCE   2  (residues 1 to 128)
  AUTHORS   Huang,R., Lin,J., Gao,D., Zhang,F., Yi,L., Huang,Y., Yan,X.,
            Duan,Y. and Zhu,X.
  TITLE     Discovery of gas vesicles in Streptomyces sp. CB03234-S and
            potential effects of gas vesicle gene overexpression on
            morphological and metabolic changes in streptomycetes
  JOURNAL   Appl Microbiol Biotechnol 103 (14), 5751-5761 (2019)
   PUBMED   31115635
  REMARK    INDUCTION, AND PROBABLE GAS VESICLE FORMATION.;
            STRAIN=CB03234
COMMENT     [FUNCTION] A minor component of the gas vesicle. May play a role in
            transcription and/or RNA stability and in GV assembly (By
            similarity). Gas vesicles are hollow, gas filled proteinaceous
            nanostructures found in some microorganisms. It is not clear what
            function gas vesicles perform in soil bacteria (Probable).
            {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O51968, ECO:0000305}.
            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Gas vesicle {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O51968}.
            [INDUCTION] Gas vesicle production is induced by growth conditions
            that promote production of secondary metabolites tiancimycin A and
            B. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:31115635}.
            [MISCELLANEOUS] This strain probably produces some gas vesicles
            from the probable gvpO-gvpA-gvpF-gvpG-gvpJ-gvpL-gvpS-gvpK operon;
            it can be induced to produce more under certain growth conditions.
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:31115635}.
            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the gas vesicle GvpO family. {ECO:0000305}.
