            Rhodococcus opacus B-4 strain was isolated as a benzene-tolerant
            bacterium (Kyung-su Na et al 2005). The complete genome analysis of
            R. opacus B-4 was carried out by NITE. The genome analysis
            indicated that this strain has one linear chromosome, two linear
            plasmids pROB01, pROB02, and three circular plasmids pKNR, pKNR01,
            pKNR02.
            
            This work was supported by New Energy and Industrial Technology
            Development Organization (NEDO).
            
            Please visit our web site.
